      ],
      "acceptable_supporting": []
    },
    "description": "DocumentPipeline, BlobStore, and Scanner expose one upload session object whose current stage is stored as a runtime field. The API allows callers to read bytes before the remote file has been opened, write after it has been committed, close it more than once, and acknowledge a checksum before scanning has completed. Existing validation reports these mistakes as runtime exceptions, and each caller implements a slightly different sequence of checks. The pipeline must support a fixed progression from creation through opening, writing, committing, scanning, and closing; each operation should be available only when its prerequisites are satisfied, and transitions should return the appropriately constrained session rather than mutating a boolean flag. Files abandoned mid-upload must remain harmless to close, while committed documents must not be modified. The application build must reject invalid operation sequences before deployment.",
    "decision_statement": "Should the upload session's lifecycle be represented in the API types so that only operations legal in the current stage can compile and each transition is checked?",
    "notes": "typestate primary: legal operations must exist only in their stage with checked type-changing transitions; type-safe-enum is the enumerated-stage near-miss."
  },
